---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import DownPaymentCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/DownPaymentCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="down-payment-calculator">
  <DownPaymentCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the down payment calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      The down payment calculator multiplies the home price by your down payment percentage, adds the closing costs
      as a percentage of the price, and gives the cash you need. The loan is the price minus the down payment.
    </p>
    <p>
      To find the time to save, your savings grow month by month: each month earns interest at
      <code>i = (1 + yearly rate)^(1/12) − 1</code> and your monthly deposit is added. The result is the first month
      in which the balance reaches the cash you need.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      For a 400,000 home with 20% down, the down payment is 80,000 and the loan is 320,000. Closing costs of 3% add
      12,000, so you need 92,000. With 30,000 saved, 1,500 a month and 4% a year on savings, you reach it in 37 months.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      The price stays the same while you save, and the savings rate is fixed and before tax. With less than 20% down,
      most conventional US loans add private mortgage insurance, which raises the monthly payment.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
